VK: no queue family indices for VK_SHARING_MODE_EXCLUSIVE images.

DeviceVK::FillCreateInfo sets queueFamilyIndexCount to the number of active families and
pQueueFamilyIndices to their indices whatever sharingMode it chose. Vulkan ignores both for
VK_SHARING_MODE_EXCLUSIVE, and the Khronos best-practices checks report
BestPractices-vkCreateImage-sharing-mode-exclusive ("pCreateInfo->sharingMode is
VK_SHARING_MODE_EXCLUSIVE while specifying multiple queues (queueFamilyIndexCount of 3)") for every
such image once more than one family is active. Measured on v190, NVIDIA, layer 1.4.341, with
graphics, compute and copy queues fetched and TextureDesc::sharingMode = EXCLUSIVE.

This passes the indices for VK_SHARING_MODE_CONCURRENT only.

diff --git a/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp b/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp
index 53f3a4d9..b041cff1 100644
--- a/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp
+++ b/Source/VK/DeviceVK.hpp
@@ -1834,8 +1834,8 @@ void DeviceVK::FillCreateInfo(const TextureDesc& textureDesc, VkImageCreateInfo&
     if ((textureDesc.usage & TextureUsageBits::HOST_TRANSFER) && m_IsSupported.hostImageCopy)
         info.usage |= VK_IMAGE_USAGE_HOST_TRANSFER_BIT_EXT;
     info.sharingMode = (m_NumActiveFamilyIndices <= 1 || textureDesc.sharingMode == SharingMode::EXCLUSIVE) ? VK_SHARING_MODE_EXCLUSIVE : VK_SHARING_MODE_CONCURRENT;
-    info.queueFamilyIndexCount = m_NumActiveFamilyIndices;
-    info.pQueueFamilyIndices = m_ActiveQueueFamilyIndices.data();
+    info.queueFamilyIndexCount = info.sharingMode == VK_SHARING_MODE_CONCURRENT ? m_NumActiveFamilyIndices : 0; // ignored for EXCLUSIVE, but validation layers warn if provided
+    info.pQueueFamilyIndices = info.sharingMode == VK_SHARING_MODE_CONCURRENT ? m_ActiveQueueFamilyIndices.data() : nullptr;
     info.initialLayout = IsMemoryZeroInitializationEnabled() ? VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_ZERO_INITIALIZED_EXT : VK_IMAGE_LAYOUT_UNDEFINED;
 }
 
